{"ISBN:9780802833501":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780802833501","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL7903690M/The_Mandaeans","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL7903690M/The_Mandaeans","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/572380-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Wm. B. Eerdmans Publishing Company"],"identifiers":{"goodreads":["503637"],"librarything":["1669938"]},"subtitle":"The Last Gnostics","weight":"1 pounds","covers":[572380],"physical_format":"Paperback","key":"/books/OL7903690M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL493808A","name":"Edmondo Lupieri"}],"subjects":["Gnosticism","Religion","Christianity - Anglican","Christianity - Anglicanism"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"first_sentence":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Soon after the Shah of Persia had been chased out and power had passed to the Ayatollah Khomeini's revolutionaries, the Mandaeans of Iran, having enjoyed complete tranquility under the secular and pro-Western government of Reza Pahlevi, thought it wise to take a precautionary measure in defense of their right to religious freedom under the new regime."},"title":"The Mandaeans","number_of_pages":304,"isbn_13":["9780802833501"],"isbn_10":["0802833500"],"publish_date":"November 30, 2001","works":[{"key":"/works/OL3126559W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"physical_dimensions":"8.9 x 5.9 x 0.9 inches","source_records":["bwb:9780802833501","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2022-03-17"],"local_id":["urn:bwbsku:P7-AUT-768"],"latest_revision":8,"revision":8,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-29T15:03:11.581851"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2023-01-14T12:08:06.628390"}}},"ISBN:9780802839244":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780802839244","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL3953364M/The_Mandaeans","preview":"restricted","preview_url":"https://archive.org/details/mandaeanslastgno0070lupi","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/572507-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["W.B. Eerdmans"],"number_of_pages":273,"subtitle":"the last gnostics","series":["Italian texts and studies on religion and society"],"covers":[572507],"local_id":["urn:cst:10011462765","urn:evs:39663100142371"],"lc_classifications":["BT1405 .L8613 2002","BT1405.L86 2001","BT1405 .L86 2002"],"key":"/books/OL3953364M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL493808A","name":"Edmondo Lupieri"}],"publish_places":["Grand Rapids, Mich"],"subjects":["Mandaeans."],"pagination":"xix, 273 p. :","source_records":["marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC2_barcode.mrc:21857097:2790","marc:marc_evangelical_seminary/Evangelical_Seminary_20200728.mrc:38315242:802","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part28.utf8:227666109:785","marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC2_multibarcode.mrc:21866732:2790","ia:mandaeanslastgno0070lupi","bwb:9780802839244","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-010.mrc:37759030:1246","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-007.mrc:238917911:2718","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_018.bib.mrc:192268428:1753"],"title":"The Mandaeans","dewey_decimal_class":["299/.932"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references (p. 53-60) and index."},"identifiers":{"goodreads":["1738017"],"librarything":["1669938"]},"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"lccn":["2001051056"],"isbn_10":["080283924X"],"publish_date":"2002","publish_country":"miu","by_statement":"Edmondo Lupieri ; translated by Charles Hindley.","work_title":["Mandei."],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL3126559W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"ocaid":"mandaeanslastgno0070lupi","oclc_numbers":["47990015"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"This book presents for the first time a complete introduction to Mandaeanism, a branch of Gnosticism that has survived to the present day.\".\n\n\"In an engaging style that mirrors the interesting nature of his subject, Edmondo Lupieri portrays the traditional way of life of the Mandaeans, still found living today in Iraq and Iran, and introduces readers to the world of Mandaean ideas - including the view that they are the only ones on earth who possess the true and oldest faith.\n\nLupieri reconstructs the history of the interaction between Mandaeanism and the Western world, beginning with Ricoldo da Montecroce, a thirteenth-century Italian monk who is the first known European to write about the Mandaeans, and continuing on to present scholarship. He also offers a critical analysis of the Mandaean written and oral traditions concerning their origin, history, and self-understanding.\".\n\n\"The book is made even more valuable by the inclusion of an extensive anthology of translated Mandaean texts, complete with notes. This collection of writings presents the spiritual world of Mandaeanism with fragments of mythical-theological texts and pages of ethical and historical meditations.\"--BOOK JACKET."},"latest_revision":15,"revision":15,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-01T03:28:50.625462"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-10-09T20:31:07.672841"}}},"ISBN:9780790593371":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780790593371","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL37897582M/Histoire_critique_du_gnosticisme","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL37897582M/Histoire_critique_du_gnosticisme","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"publish_date":"1843","publish_country":"fr","languages":[{"key":"/languages/fre"}],"authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL1676439A","name":"Jacques Matter"}],"edition_name":"2. éd., rev. et augm.","series":["ATLA monograph preservation program -- ATLA fiche 1989-2562."],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"Ouvrage couronné par l'Académie royale des inscriptions et belles-lettres.\"\n\nFirst printed in 1828, 2 v.\n\nMicrofiche. Evanston : American Theological Library Association, 1991. 3 microfiche. High reduction. Silver based film. (ATLA monograph preservation program ; ATLA fiche 1989-2562)"},"subjects":["Gnosticism","Church history